{"niyata": [{"id": "niyata", "headword": "नियत", "headword_slp1": "niyata", "fold": "niyata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियत [niyata], p. p.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Curbed, restrained; तं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया Bg.7.2.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Subdued, controlled, self-possessed, self-governed.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Abstemious, temperate.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Attentive, intent.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Fixed, permanent, constant, steady; अन्यथासिद्धिशून्यस्य नियता पूर्ववर्तिता Bhāṣā. P.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(a) Certain, settled, sure; Pt.1.284. (b) Fixed; प्रकृतिनियतत्वादकृतकः U.6.14; fixed in number, limited; बाणाः पञ्च मनोभवस्य नियतास्तेषामसंख्यो जनः (लक्ष्यः) Ratn.3.3.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Inevitable.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Positive, definite.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Forming the subject of consideration, relevant or irrelevant; see तुल्ययोगिता.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Maintained, observed (as a vow &c.); नियतैकपतिव्रतानि पश्चात्तरुमूलानि गृहीभवन्ति तेषाम् Ś.7.2.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Held back, fastened, tied; पशूनां त्रिशतं तत्र यूपेषु नियतं तदा Rām.1.14.32.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Connected with, dependent on; वाच्यर्था नियताः सर्वे Ms.4.256.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(in gram.) Pronounced with अनुदात्त. -तम् (pl.) (in Sāṅkhya) the organs of sense. -तम् ind.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Always, constantly.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Positively, certainly, invariably, inevitably, surely.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Forcibly.-Comp. -काल a. Limited in time, temporary; Kaśi. on P.I.4.44. -मानस a. of subdued mind. -वाच a. limited as to the use of words. -व्रत a. pious, religious.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyata"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyata"]}], "niyatiH": [{"id": "niyatiH", "headword": "नियतिः", "headword_slp1": "niyatiH", "fold": "niyatiH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियतिः [niyatiḥ], f.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Restraint, restriction.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Destiny, fate, luck, fortune (good or bad); (sometimes personified as a goddess, the sister of Āyati, both being daughters of Meru and wives of Dhātṛi and Vidhātṛi); नियति- बलान्नु Dk.; नियतेर्नियोगात् Śi.4.34; Ki.2.12;4.21.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A religious duty or obligation; नियतिः कारणं लोके नियतिः कर्मसाधनम् । नियतिः सर्वभूतानां नियोगोष्बिह कारणम् ॥ Rām.4.25. 4.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Self-command, self-restraint.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyati", "niyatiH", "niyatiḥ", "नियति"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyati", "niyatiH", "niyatiḥ", "niyati"]}], "niyantf": [{"id": "niyantf", "headword": "नियन्तृ", "headword_slp1": "niyantf", "fold": "niyantf", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियन्तृ [niyantṛ], m.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A charioteer, driver; नियन्तरि व्याकुलमुक्त- रज्जुके Śi.12.24.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A governor, ruler, master, regulator; न व्यतीयुः प्रजास्तस्य नियन्तुर्नेमिवृत्तयः R.1.17;15.51.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A punisher, chastiser.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "The Supreme Being.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyantR", "niyantṛ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyantR", "niyantṛ"]}], "niyantraRam": [{"id": "niyantraRam", "headword": "नियन्त्रणम्", "headword_slp1": "niyantraRam", "fold": "niyantraRam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियन्त्रणम् [niyantraṇam] णा [ṇā], णा 1 Checking, reserve, restraint; अनि- यन्त्रणानुयोगो नाम तपस्विजनः Ś.1.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Restricting, confining (to a particular sense); अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्यैकार्थ- नियन्त्रणम् S. D.2.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Guiding, governing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Defining.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyantraNa", "niyantraNam", "niyantraṇa", "niyantraṇam", "नियन्त्रण"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyantraNa", "niyantraNam", "niyantraṇa", "niyantraṇam", "niyantraRa"]}], "niyantrita": [{"id": "niyantrita", "headword": "नियन्त्रित", "headword_slp1": "niyantrita", "fold": "niyantrita", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियन्त्रित [niyantrita], p. p. Curbed, restrained, checked.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Guided, governed.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Restricted, confined to (a particular sense, as a word).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyantrita"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyantrita"]}], "niyamaH": [{"id": "niyamaH", "headword": "नियमः", "headword_slp1": "niyamaH", "fold": "niyamaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "नियमः [niyamḥ], 1 Restraining, checking.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Taming, subduing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Confining, preventing.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A restraint, check; वाचि नियमः U.2.2; अधर्मानियमः Ms.8.122.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Restriction, limitation; Mb.14.13.11.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A rule or precept, law (in general), usage; नायमेकान्ततो नियमः Ś. B.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Regularity; कुसुमसुकुमारमूर्तिर्दधती नियमेन तनुतरं मध्यम् Ratn. 1.2.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Certainty, ascertainment.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "An agreement, promise, vow, engagement.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Necessity, obligation.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Any voluntary or self-imposed religious observance (dependent on external conditions); [The earliest explanation of this expression is the one found in the ŚB. on MS.4.2.24. cf. को$यं नियमः । अनियतस्य नियतता । प्रयोगाङ्गतया सर्वे देशाः प्राप्नुवन्ति, न तु समच्चयेन । यदा समो न तदा विषमः । यदा विषमो न तदा समः । स एष समः प्राप्तश्चाप्राप्तश्च । यदा न प्राप्तः स पक्षो विधिं प्रयोजयति. This is very nicely stated in the Vārttika'नियमः पाक्षिके सति']; R.1.94; Ki.5.4; (see Malli. on Śi.13.23).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Any minor observance or lesser vow, a duty prescribed to be done, but which is not so obligatory as a यम q. v. शौचमिज्या तपो दानं स्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहः । व्रतमौनोपवासं च स्नानं च नियमा दशा ॥ Atri.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Penance, devotion, religious austerities; नियमविघ्न- कारिणी Ś.1; R.15.74.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(In Mīm. phil.) A rule or precept which lays down or specifies something which, in the absence of that rule, would be optional; विधिरत्यन्तमप्राप्तौ नियमः पाक्षिके सति.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(In Yoga phil.) Restraint of the mind, the second of the 8 principal steps of meditation in Yoga; दशैते नियमाः प्रोक्ता योगशास्त्र- विशारदैः Tantrasāra.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(In Rhet.) A poetical commonp lace or convention, as the description of the cuckoo in spring, peacocks in the rains &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Defining, definition.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Keeping down, lowering (as the voice).", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Keeping secret; मन्त्रस्य नियमं कुर्याः Mb.5. 141.2.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Effort (यत्न); यथैते नियमं पौराः कुर्वन्त्यस्मिन्निवर्तने Mb.2.46.2. (नियमेन as a rule, invariably). -Comp. -उपमा a simile which expressly states that something can be compared only with something else. -धर्मः a law prescribing restraints. -निष्ठा rigid observance of prescribed rites. -पत्रम् a written agreement. -विधिः a religious rite, daily ritual; नियमविधिजलानां बर्हिषां चोप- नेत्री Ku.1.6. -स्थ a. observing penance; Ku.5.13.-स्थितिः f. steady observance of religious obligations, asceticism. -हेतुः a regulating cause.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["niyama", "niyamaH", "niyamaḥ", "नियम"], "synonyms_slp1": ["niyama", "ni